<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5791" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">buccŭla</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">būcŭla</span></b> ), ae,
			f.
		dim.
		bucca. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A little cheek</i> or <i>mouth</i>,
			* <i><span class="en">Suet. Galb. 4</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pressa Cupidinis buccula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 6, p. 182, 17</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">3</span></i>, p. 137, 40; <i><span class="en">Arn. 2,
				p. 73</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In milit. lang. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>The beaver</i>, <i>that part of a
				helmet which covers the mouth and cheeks</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραγναθίς</span>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bucculas tergere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					44, 34, 8</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Juv. 10, 134</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Capitol. Max. Jun. 3</span></i>; Cod. Th. 10,
			22, 1.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Bucculae, <i>two cheeks</i>, <i>one on
				each side of the channel in which the arrow of the catapulta was
				placed</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 10, 15, 3</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
